    "long_instructions": "*This level follows a video that you may have watched with your class. If you missed the video, you can watch it [here](https://youtu.be/q7d_JtyCq1A).*\r\n\r\n# Welcome to Web Lab!\r\n\r\nThe platform you are in is called Web Lab. There are three main parts of the screen in Web Lab.\r\n\r\n![Web Lab Panels](https://images.code.org/01885e46c31f369f9509bd3c7529543c-WEBLAB2%20tour%201%20(1).png)\r\n\r\nIn this level, let's get to know our partner for pair programming.\r\n\r\n# Do This\r\n\r\n**Driver:**\r\n\r\nType the name of your Navigator, their favorite color, and their favorite animal on different lines in the workspace.\r\n    \r\n::: details [**Show Me How**]\r\n![Where to type code](https://images.code.org/ba30161cfa3f8d08cd77f16b0e656116-ezgif-2bc615e4774269f0.gif)    \r\n:::\r\n\r\n&nbsp;\r\n\r\nDoes the preview match how you typed it in the workspace?",
    "teacher_markdown": "After giving students some time to explore the tool, ask them to share out anything that they have discovered.  The video on the next level will give them a short tour, so it's okay if they don't notice everything.",
